      "JS executes supported public special-loader level_init, gas_cloud, ladder, exclusion and reset_level APIs; no private JS extraction or mutation of resource heads. Initial list lengths are asserted. C exact reset/clear and all three cleanup routines plus free_region execute over owned, valid allocated metadata. C fixture construction is a typed allocation adapter, not independent C descriptor constructors.",
      "C region records own a rect allocation; messages and monster arrays are null. Stair/exclusion records carry only fields used by cleanup. Geometry/metadata content is not compared. Absent-resource reset preparation and unrelated helpers are adapters; only final logical cleanup is proven. C malloc/free success is assumed; no OOM, allocator-size, resource ownership outside the fixture or JS GC/reclamation timing claim.",
      "Region comparison maps C count/capacity/null array to JS empty active list/capacity0; this is logical absence, not pointer representation equality. Stair/exclusion linked heads are null after both resets. Other resource types, flags, frames, topology and reset effects are not included.",
